diff --git a/frontend/src/ui/AGENTS.md b/frontend/src/ui/AGENTS.md
index 7f933fd..5be0071 100644
--- a/frontend/src/ui/AGENTS.md
+++ b/frontend/src/ui/AGENTS.md
@@ -10,7 +10,9 @@ Resizing (plan §2 #84): `ResizeDots.vue` draws the three dots of every resize h
 
 Questions (`asking.ts`): one at a time; `ask` resolves `"yes" | "no" | "dismissed"` (Escape is `dismiss`, a second `ask` while one waits is dismissed at once). Callers whose Escape means cancel compare `=== "yes"`. A question about the stop (`question.ts` `endsWithStop`: Mark resolved's, Abort's) is dismissed when the stop ends; the others stay.
 
-Listing and stops (plan §2 #87–#89): every list is `listing.ts` `refreshFiles` over `listStop`, the only writer of `files`, `operation` and `sideNames`, all from one reply; `MovedOn` goes to `nextStop`. `stops.ts` `nextStop` ends a stop: it bumps `latestOpen`, drops the stop (`saving.ts` `dropStop`: the `Stop` token marked dropped, every claim overtaken and gone), dismisses the stop's question, clears every per-stop state (opened files, choices, taken, notices, format notes, the shown file, the problem, git's stop message `stopMessage`, the screen) and lists as at start; `outside` with unsaved edits adds the one moved-on notice, `continued` to an empty stop the `stopped` problem and git's message as `stopMessage`, kept for the whole stop. "A reply after the stop was dropped changes nothing" is written once, `currentStop.ts` (`Stop`, `landed(stop, call)`: null once dropped): every write, the format step, Abort, Continue and every reload (`views.ts` `reload`, also for disk changes, `diskChanges.ts` `applyDiskChanges`) capture `target.stop` before they call. A failure answered `StopMovedOn` is reported through `problem.ts` `reportFailure`, which lists again. `operationText.ts` holds every operation word (the top line and its tooltip, Continue's and Abort's labels, Continue's hover, Abort's title and question); `OperationBar.vue` shows the top line above the notices while git records an operation.
+Listing and stops (plan §2 #87–#89): every list is `listing.ts` `refreshFiles` over `listStop`, the only writer of `files`, `operation` and `sideNames`, all from one reply; `MovedOn` goes to `nextStop`. `stops.ts` `nextStop` ends a stop: it bumps `latestOpen`, drops the stop (`saving.ts` `dropStop`: the `Stop` token marked dropped, every claim overtaken and gone), dismisses the stop's question, clears every per-stop state (opened files, choices, taken, notices, format notes, the shown file, the problem, git's stop message `stopMessage`, the screen) and lists as at start; `outside` with unsaved edits adds the one moved-on notice, `continued` to an empty stop the `stopped` problem and git's message as `stopMessage`, kept for the whole stop. "A reply after the stop was dropped changes nothing" is written once, `currentStop.ts` (`Stop`, `landed(stop, call)`: null once dropped): every write, the format step, Abort, Continue and every reload (`views.ts` `reload`, also for disk changes, `diskChanges.ts` `applyDiskChanges`) capture `target.stop` before they call. `StopMovedOn` always means the stop the window shows is gone (#1435): a list answered after it would only open the new stop under the old views, so every failure answered `StopMovedOn` goes to `nextStop({ outside })` — the writes, Abort, an open and every reload through `problem.ts` `reportFailure` (logged, no problem shown; its target asks only for `nextStop`), Continue in `continuing.ts`. `operationText.ts` holds every operation word (the top line and its tooltip, Continue's and Abort's labels, Continue's hover, Abort's title and question); `OperationBar.vue` shows the top line above the notices while git records an operation.
+
+File marks (plan §2 #90): `FileMark.vue` renders a file's name and its mark in the list and the tree from one table per `FileStatus` (`Unresolved` none; `Resolved` the check and a muted name; `Remembered` the history icon with the rerere hint as its title and accessible name); `FileList.vue` and `FileTree.vue` pass only the status and the label.
 
 Git running (plan §2 #74, #89): `gitRun.ts` `createGitRun` is the one owner of "git is running": `run(stop, { call, endsApp, landing })` sets `running`, calls through `landed`, lands the reply while still running, and clears it unless the reply is a success that ends the app (`endsApp`: every Abort success, Continue's `Finished`). Abort, Continue and `closeGuard.ts` only read `running`; while it is set `mayClose` refuses with the `close` problem and asks nothing.
 
